  "summary": "n8n helper node executes host recon at install and require time",
  "details": "The package's postinstall hook runs a Node one-liner that shell-executes `id` and `hostname` and writes the output to `/tmp/pwned.txt` on `npm install`. The main entry point `index.js` executes at require time and runs `id; hostname; uname -a; ls -la /home; cat /etc/hostname` via child_process.execSync, writing the result to `/tmp/n8n_pwned.txt`; a source comment states this runs inside the n8n main process with no sandbox. The declared n8n node's execute() function additionally runs `id; hostname; uname -a; ls -la /home; ls -la /` and returns the output as node results, with the node self-labeled `pwned`. Installing or loading this package causes unauthorized shell execution and host reconnaissance on the installer's machine.",
